(S, "Fill in the preposition: He waited ___ the station.", ["at", "on", "to", "by"], 0, "We use at with a place regarded as a point, such as a station.", "Waited for is used with the thing or person awaited, such as waited for the train.", [1715]),
(S, "Which is the highest railway station in Pakistan, at about 2,224 metres above sea level?", ["Kan Mehtarzai", "Khanai", "Lahore Junction", "Rohri"], 0, "Kan Mehtarzai on the Zhob Valley Railway in Balochistan is cited as Pakistan's highest railway station.", "The line is closed since 1986 and Kan Mehtarzai is no longer in use.", [3793]),
